<li><p class='igt' id='i80'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/81.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i80w'><span class="word" id="i80w0">Ting</span><span class="word" id="i80w1">xothq'idz</span><span class="word" id="i80w2">didlang</span><span class="word" id="i80w3">chux</span><span class="word" id="i80w4">xindighe'o.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i80g'><span class="gloss" id="i80g0">trail</span><span class="gloss" id="i80g1">alongside</span><span class="gloss" id="i80g2">spruce</span><span class="gloss" id="i80g3">big</span><span class="gloss" id="i80g4">it stands</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i80ft'>'Beside the trail stood a big spruce tree.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i81'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/82.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i81w'><span class="word" id="i81w0">Yitlyiɬ.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i81g'><span class="gloss" id="i81g0">she grabbed onto it</span><span class="gloss" id="i81g1"></span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i81ft'>'She grabbed onto it.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i82'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/83.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i82w'><span class="word" id="i82w0">Ngidiggi</span><span class="word" id="i82w1">didlang</span><span class="word" id="i82w2">q'idz</span><span class="word" id="i82w3">xitl'uggok.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i82g'><span class="gloss" id="i82g0">upward</span><span class="gloss" id="i82g1">spruce</span><span class="gloss" id="i82g2">on</span><span class="gloss" id="i82g3">she ran up</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i82ft'>'She ran up the spruce tree.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i83'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/84.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i83w'><span class="word" id="i83w0">Xiyghoyix</span><span class="word" id="i83w1">xizro</span><span class="word" id="i83w2">gits'anxodiɬ.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i83g'><span class="gloss" id="i83g0">they beneath her</span><span class="gloss" id="i83g1">only</span><span class="gloss" id="i83g2">they're encircling</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i83ft'>'They encircled it beneath her.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i84'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/85.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i84w'><span class="word" id="i84w0">Ngidiggits'i</span><span class="word" id="i84w1">xiyniɬ'anh</span><span class="word" id="i84w2">ts'ixizro.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i84g'><span class="gloss" id="i84g0">upward</span><span class="gloss" id="i84g1">they looked</span><span class="gloss" id="i84g2">only</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i84ft'>'They looked upward.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i85'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/86.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i85w'><span class="word" id="i85w0">Uxuxuyiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i85w1">digitthigits'igh</span><span class="word" id="i85w2">yadz tidhu'onh.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i85g'><span class="gloss" id="i85g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i85g1">her hood</span><span class="gloss" id="i85g2">she pushed back</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i85ft'>'Then she pushed back her hood.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i86'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/87.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i86w'><span class="word" id="i86w0">&quot;Seghaye,&quot;</span><span class="word" id="i86w1">xiɬne,</span><span class="word" id="i86w2">&quot;gila'</span><span class="word" id="i86w3">ghinoy</span><span class="word" id="i86w4">uxlayh</span><span class="word" id="i86w5">tux</span><span class="word" id="i86w6">soxo</span><span class="word" id="i86w7">gichot</span><span class="word" id="i86w8">xizro</span><span class="word" id="i86w9">niguxlayh,&quot;</span><span class="word" id="i86w10">xiɬne.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i86g'><span class="gloss" id="i86g0">my brothers</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g1">she said to them</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g2">now</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g3">caribou</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g4">you pl. kill</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g5">when</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g6">for me</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g7">guts</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g8">only</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g9">you pl. leave</span><span class="gloss" id="i86g10">she said to them</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i86ft'>&quot;'My brothers,&quot; she said to them, &quot;from now on when you kill caribou, leave only the guts for me.&quot;'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i87'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/88.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i87w'><span class="word" id="i87w0">Uxuxiyiɬ</span><span class="word" id="i87w1">xiygho ntithidatl.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i87g'><span class="gloss" id="i87g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i87g1">they left her</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i87ft'>'Then they left her.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i88'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/89.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i88w'><span class="word" id="i88w0">Yitots'in'</span><span class="word" id="i88w1">nonghidiyo</span><span class="word" id="i88w2">nuq'oɬonh.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i88g'><span class="gloss" id="i88g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i88g1">she came down</span><span class="gloss" id="i88g2">woman</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i88ft'>'Then the woman came down.'</span></p></li>
<li><p class='igt' id='i89'><a href="//depts.washington.edu/dxmedia/Chapman/4__Nil-treth_Veghaye/mp3/90.mp3" class='audio'>hidden</a><span class='words' id='i89w'><span class="word" id="i89w0">Yitots'i</span><span class="word" id="i89w1">idedig</span><span class="word" id="i89w2">gidegh</span><span class="word" id="i89w3">tadhiyo.</span></span><br /><span class='glosses' id='i89g'><span class="gloss" id="i89g0">then</span><span class="gloss" id="i89g1">she too</span><span class="gloss" id="i89g2">away</span><span class="gloss" id="i89g3">she went</span></span><br /><span class='trans' id='i89ft'>'And she too went away.'</span></p></li>
</ol></div><div id='notes'><h2>Notes</h2><ol><li><span class="footnote" id="n1">Chapman/Kari have <em> giɬigg </em> 'one' as the first word of the sentence.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n2">JD says <em> noxidelanh. </em> The sound <em> n </em> is often deleted before the sound <em> x.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n3">Chapman/Kari have <em> yan' </em> 'only' after <em> nelang.</em></span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n4">The second sentence was not recorded.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n5">Chapman's version of the song is given here. JD did not know it.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n6">Again, the song is Chapman's. JD does not sing it.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n7">Chapman's version has <em> yûkû </em> 'there' as the first word of the sentence, which makes more sense in terms of the story. He gives the verb as <em> qaiyûkûxaidätl </em> 'they went there'. Kari deciphered this as <em> xuyexighedatl </em> 'they went in'.</span></li><li><span class="footnote" id="n8">JD's recorded title is <em> Niɬtreth Vegha </em> 'Wolverine's older brother'</span></li></ol>
</div>
</div>
</body>
